/**
 * @file documentation_guide.dox
 * @brief Guided entry page for users and developers reading the generated docs.
 *
 * @page documentation_guide Documentation guide and reading paths
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section docs_goal Goal of this guide
 *
 * This page helps readers choose a sensible path through the generated
 * documentation instead of jumping directly into the raw class and file
 * indexes. The repository serves two audiences:
 *
 * - users who need to write and validate SPL files in the repository DSL,
 * - developers who need to understand the parser, analysis pipeline, and
 *   isolation implementation.
 *
 * @section docs_user_track User path: authoring an SPL file
 *
 * Read these pages in order if your goal is to create or understand an SPL
 * input file:
 *
 * 1. @ref spl_authoring_guide
 * 2. @ref spl_examples_guide
 * 3. @ref spl_parser
 *
 * This path explains the full DSL structure, valid section usage, operator
 * rules, availability annotations, reporting filters, worked examples, and the
 * parser-backed executable semantics.
 *
 * @section docs_dev_track Developer path: implementation overview
 *
 * Read these pages in order if your goal is to understand how the repository
 * executes the DSL and performs analysis:
 *
 * 1. @ref spl_parser
 * 2. @ref feature_analysis
 * 3. @ref feature_isolation
 * 4. @ref fi_mathhelper
 *
 * This path takes you from parsing and system-space derivation to derived
 * feature construction, isolation witnesses, and the arithmetic helpers used by
 * the implementation.
 *
 * @section docs_reference_track API reference path
 *
 * After the guided pages above, use the generated reference views for exact
 * type and function behavior:
 *
 * - Classes
 * - Files
 * - Namespaces
 * - File Members
 *
 * The guided pages explain intent and workflow. The reference views document
 * the exact symbols that implement those workflows.
 *
 * @section docs_related Key destination pages
 *
 * - @ref spl_authoring_guide
 * - @ref spl_examples_guide
 * - @ref spl_parser
 * - @ref feature_analysis
 * - @ref feature_isolation
 * - @ref fi_mathhelper
 */